# AGENTS.md — `lab/` (wet-lab records)

Root `../AGENTS.md` applies. Human orientation: [`README.md`](README.md).

This folder records what happened at the bench. It is **provenance about the
physical world**, and an agent cannot observe the physical world.

## Hard rule
**Do not fabricate.** Never invent or fill in sample manifests, protocol steps,
reagent lots, measurements, dates, or results. If information is missing, ask the
user or leave it blank — never guess. Inventing bench records corrupts provenance
for the whole project.

## You may
- Reformat or reorganize existing human-provided notes without changing their content.
- Help draft a protocol *template* the user will fill in with real values.
- Cross-check that `../metadata/` manifests are consistent with notes here and flag
  discrepancies (don't silently "fix" them).

The ELN is the system of record; treat this folder as the repo-side pointer to it.
